From 41825bd403107dfc7f7eebf9cd89319174c85674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 18:06:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen all three censuses past the suites they could reach
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Item 2-13 said this engine's largest private deficiency is zlib, 12.0x behind
Jint relative to Chromium. Asking what the censuses say about it turned up that
none of the three can answer, for two different reasons.

TypeFeedbackMetrics and SpecializingTierMetrics both ran seven of Octane's
fifteen suites, and the roadmap quotes their output as "the corpus" — the phrase
every phase-3 and phase-4 headline uses — over a denominator it never states.
PropertyMapDistributionMetrics lists all fifteen and reaches nine: it aborts on
Mandreel and, serializing only at the end, emits nothing at all when it does. So
items 2-7 and 2-9's map figures were not reproducible from a clean tree; the
only way to get output was BROILER_MAP_DISTRIBUTION_SKIP, and the recorded
numbers do not say what was skipped.

The abort is the same in all three: Mandreel's global_init overflows the stack
uncatchably, because item 0-2's 16 MiB thread and 4 MiB reserve are a property
of Broiler.JavaScript/Program.cs — the shell — and the benchmark hosts built
plain contexts on whatever stack the runtime handed Main. Every benchmark host
in this campaign has been running without the reserve the shell has had since
phase 0.

All three now run on the shell's thread with the shell's MaxStackUsageBytes and
checkpoint after every suite, so an abort keeps what ran. Mandreel fails the way
the shell makes it fail, catchably. TypeFeedbackMetrics also emits its corpus
aggregate with the suite count beside it, rather than leaving it to be totalled
by whoever quotes it.

Each widened count reproduces its old value over the old suites, so each is the
same instrument over more of them:

  reads, monomorphic   93.54% of 37.9 M  ->  80.11% of 307.9 M
  calls, monomorphic   96.70% of 4.24 M  ->  86.35% of 52.9 M
  boxes allocated         31,401,346     ->     90,641,738
  allocated bytes            3.13 GB     ->       12.93 GB
  property maps                    —     ->      2,202,782

87.7% of the corpus's reads and 65.4% of its boxes were outside the seven.
Gameboy — never in a census — is 34.60% monomorphic with 1 282 polymorphic
sites and allocates 41.3 M boxes on its own, 1.32x the whole previously
measured corpus. 2-9 is corroborated at 2.2 M maps. 2-7 splits: live memory
still favours the shipped policy but by less than recorded (0.644x against
0.56x), while its allocated-bytes win changes sign, 0.82x becoming 1.044x,
because geometric growth pays 33x the node copying on suites it never saw.

Two instrument defects are surfaced rather than fixed silently: the policy table
still labels round-up-16 "current" though 2-7 replaced it, and one histogram
bucket reads -15, so negativeBucketCounts now ships in the output.

